id: rule-if-branch-fails
title: A branch fails
topic: Conditional
example-of: IF
derived: false

task:
  Use the rule IF to try to derive this triple. Each branch is checked
  with the rule ASSIGN and the consequence rule.

given:
  Condition B: $x > 0$

pre: true
post: y > 0

scheme: IF
  Then branch: {«P» && «x > 0 : B»} y := x {«Q»}
  Else branch: {«P» && «!(x > 0) : ¬B»} y := 0 {«Q»}
  ---
  {«P»} if x > 0 then y := x else y := 0 {«Q»}

program:
  {P}
  if x > 0 then {
    {P && x > 0}
    {R1}
    y := x       // then
    {Q}
  } else {
    {P && !(x > 0)}
    {R2}
    y := 0       // else
    {Q}
  }
  {Q}

verdict: invalid

step: R1, the weakest precondition of y := x
part: Then branch
rule: ASSIGN
focus: then
text:
  We substitute the variable $y$ with $x$ in $Q$.
calc:
  wp(y := x, Q)
  = (y > 0)[y <- x]     // Q is y > 0
  = x > 0               // y replaced by x
set: R1 = x > 0

step: P and B imply R1
part: Then branch
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: P && x > 0, R1
text:
  >>> «P» && «x > 0 : B» ==> «R1»
vc: true && x > 0 ==> x > 0
why:
  $R1$ is the condition $B$ itself.

step: R2, the weakest precondition of y := 0
part: Else branch
rule: ASSIGN
focus: else
text:
  We substitute the variable $y$ with $0$ in $Q$.
calc:
  wp(y := 0, Q)
  = (y > 0)[y <- 0]     // Q is y > 0
  = 0 > 0               // y replaced by 0
  = false               // 0 > 0 is false
set: R2 = false

step: P and not B do not imply R2
part: Else branch
rule: CONSEQUENCE
focus: P && !(x > 0), R2
text:
  >>> «P» && «!(x > 0) : ¬B» ==> «R2»
vc: true && !(x > 0) ==> false
status: fails
counterexample: x = 0
why:
  The state $x = 0$ satisfies the left side. From it the else branch sets
  $y$ to 0, so $Q$ is false at the end. The triple is not valid.
